{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` is package data imported by path: `_loader.py::lazy_load`, 44 in-package loader prologues, hand-rolled loaders in twelve engine modules (cited in this ticket's first comment), and the out-of-package loaders `_lib_ops._engine_module` (`:161-173`), `_bridge_commands._ref_lock_module` (`:147-161`), `mcp_server._load_engine_mode` (`:367-378`, the `rebar._engine_mode` fork), `_engine.engine_env`'s PYTHONPATH prepend (`:75-102`) and four `sys.path.insert` sites (step 5). The generic top-level name violates namespace hygiene (`docs/architecture.md:244-272`), the by-path idiom forces a `sys.modules` key contract onto 343 test files (442 `spec_from_file_location` sites), and mypy widens every `rebar_reconciler.` annotation to `Any` (`pyproject.toml:627-634`). Operator decision (2026-09-06), BREAKING: the package becomes `rebar.reconciler` with no re-export shim (ADR 0083, ADR 0111); `python -m rebar.reconciler` replaces `python -m rebar_reconciler`; `engine_env` stops prepending `PYTHONPATH`. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\n1. `git mv src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler src/rebar/reconciler`. A throwaway local codemod rewrites, in `src`, `scripts`, `infra`, `tests`: `from rebar_reconciler`, `import rebar_reconciler`, quoted `\"rebar_reconciler\"` and `\"rebar_reconciler.<x>\"` strings (including the argv element at `_cli/_bridge_commands.py:51`), and the bare tokens `rebar_reconciler` and `rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler` inside docstrings and comments (`src/rebar/timeutils.py:9,11`, `src/rebar/_proc.py:7`, `src/rebar/_operation_config.py:232`, `_bridge_commands.py:32`, and the in-package prose), all to `rebar.reconciler`.\n2. Delete `_loader.py`; delete every `try/except ImportError` loader prologue and every `lazy_load(...)`/`_load_*` call, replacing each with a plain `from rebar.reconciler import x` at module scope, function-local where a cycle exists, keeping the same names so `monkeypatch.setattr` targets survive. In `__main__.py` delete `_load_sibling_keyed` (`:116-139`) and `_try_load_step` (`:141-160`) with their call sites at `:315,344,358,367,417,493,494,529`, the reconcile-absent no-op branch at `:344-348` and the `_advisory is None` fallback at `:364-371`.\n3. Delete the `__main__.py:49-56` bootstrap fallback; `install_stderr_handler(\"rebar_reconciler\")` at `:491` becomes `\"rebar\"`; delete the `__init__.py` NullHandler (the `rebar` root has one).\n4. `src/rebar/_engine.py::engine_env` (`:75-102`): drop the PYTHONPATH prepend; it only pins `REBAR_ROOT`. `engine_dir()` stays for `jira-capability-probe.py` and `resources/`, its docstring and error text no longer naming the reconciler.\n5. Delete `_lib_ops._engine_module` and rewrite its consumers: `_lib_ops.py` imports `rebar.reconciler.{projects_store,pass_support,__main__,mode,last_pass,_ref_lock,access_check}` directly; `_commands/bridge_repair.py:158-160` becomes `from rebar.reconciler import binding_store`; `_bridge_commands.py:147-161` (`_ref_lock_module`) and `:188-189` become `from rebar.reconciler import _ref_lock, last_pass`; `mcp_server.py:359-378,599-600` deleted (no registrar reads `ctx.MODE_CAPS`/`ctx.Mode`; `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py:130-131` and `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py:97-98` drop the two kwargs); `_bridge_runner.py:146-151` becomes `from rebar.reconciler.__main__ import _Disposition`; the `sys.path.insert` sites `_cli/__init__.py:144-151`, `_commands/{_repair_pause.py:37-42,doctor_mapping.py:41-45,fsck_repair.py:342-347}` and the loaders in `_engine_support/bridge_fsck_{drift.py:31-35,visibility.py:28-50}` become plain imports; `src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py:25-26` imports `rebar.reconciler.*`.\n6. Eight scripts that hardcode the directory are re-pointed to `src/rebar/reconciler` (the list with line cites, and the scripts verified untouched, are in this ticket's first comment).\n7. `pyproject.toml:567` per-file T201 ignore becomes `\"src/rebar/reconciler/*\"`; comments at `:14,68,509,613,627-634` updated; no hatch change.\n8. Tests (mechanical only): every `spec_from_file_location(<key>, <engine path>)` helper becomes `importlib.import_module(\"rebar.reconciler.<mod>\")`; every `sys.modules[...]` seed, `_ENGINE_DIR` and `sys.path.insert` is deleted; `patch(\"rebar_reconciler.x.y\")` strings become `\"rebar.reconciler.x.y\"`; tests that needed a fresh module copy use `monkeypatch.setattr` on the shared module (`importlib.reload` of `rebar.reconciler.*` is forbidden). `tests/_engine_path.py` keeps only `repo_root()` (engine functions deleted by the next story). `tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py:27` assertion on `_engine/rebar_reconciler` removed.\n9. Docs: the eight maintained docs and `README.md` listed with line cites in the first comment spell `python -m rebar.reconciler` and `rebar.reconciler`; `CHANGELOG.md` BREAKING entry; regenerate `docs/env-vars.md` with `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py`.\n10. `.github/complexity-baseline.json`: re-spell the 6 engine keys to `src/rebar/reconciler/...` with ceilings unchanged and the map RE-SORTED (`reconciler/` sorts after the underscore-prefixed keys; an unsorted file fails `--check`); an operator-sanctioned maintenance edit recorded on the epic and restated in the commit message. The CI lock step rejects the six added keys by design; the operator force-submits this one change (landing instruction in the comments).\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/reconciler/**` (moved), `src/rebar/_engine.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py`, `src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py`, `src/rebar/mcp_server.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py` (lines 144-151 only; the CLI epic owns the rest), `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/{_repair_pause,doctor_mapping,fsck_repair,bridge_repair}.py`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_{drift,visibility}.py`, prose-only edits in `src/rebar/{timeutils.py,_proc.py,_operation_config.py,_logging.py,_config_schema.py}`, `.github/complexity-baseline.json`, the scripts, docs, and tests listed above. Out of scope: `_config_sources.py`, `config.py`, `_deprecations.py` (config epic); the rest of `_cli/` (CLI epic); the test-side loader complex and the test-package rename (next story); every behavioural change to the engine.\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `python -c \"import rebar.reconciler, rebar.reconciler.__main__\"`; `python -m rebar.reconciler --help` exits 0 with no PYTHONPATH; `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler tests/interfaces tests/scripts -q`; `make import-walk`; `make typecheck` (fix newly resolvable annotation errors at site; add no `ignore_missing_imports`). Edge: `git grep -nE 'rebar_reconciler|lazy_load\\(|_engine/rebar_reconciler' -- src scripts infra tests` returns only frozen fixture corpora under `tests/fixtures/`, and the same grep over `docs README.md ':!docs/adr' ':!docs/experiments' ':!docs/archive'` returns nothing; `python -c \"import rebar, rebar_reconciler\"` fails (`tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py::test_library_path_exposes_no_generic_top_level_engine_names` still passes); `test_transport_param_typing_cc77.py` updated for the now-checkable port annotations; `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` prints `new=0 increased=0`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` and `_loader.py` do not exist and `src/rebar/reconciler/__init__.py` exists, verified by `git ls-tree`.\n- [ ] `git grep -nE 'spec_from_file_location|lazy_load\\(' -- src` returns only the `src/rebar/graph/_loader.py` docstring, and the two edge greps above are empty.\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.reconciler preview --repo-root <tmp>` runs from a fresh venv with no `PYTHONPATH` (the `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py` subprocess case).\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0; `.github/complexity-baseline.json` has 6 sorted `src/rebar/reconciler/` keys with unchanged ceilings (`check_complexity_baseline.py --check` prints `new=0 increased=0`).\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` is clean."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788814675076134242,"uuid":"fd4a737f-6293-44cc-879f-40e5c02392d0"}